      "content": "Senior Turkish Delegation Visits Somalia as Bilateral Cooperation Expands | Horseed Media Skip to content Search Home Somalia News Puntland News World News in English Featured More.. Dowladda Federaalka Galmudug Hiiraan News Jubaland News Koonfur Galbeed SSC Somaliland Follow us Search News Somalia Senior Turkish Delegation Visits Somalia as Bilateral Cooperation Expands Posted by: Horseed Staff A senior Turkish delegation led by Fatih Dulkan, vice-president of the Turkish Space Agency, has arrived in Somalia as cooperation between the two countries expands into space, technology and industry. 25 October, 2026 Share Tweet The delegation includes officials from Türkiye’s Ministry of Industry and Technology, the country’s defence industry sector and defence company Roketsan. During the visit, the Turkish officials held meetings with Somali counterparts and inspected ongoing activities in Mogadishu and Warsheikh. The visit highlights the growing scope of the Somalia-Türkiye partnership, which has expanded beyond traditional areas of cooperation to include space technology, industrial development, technology and defence industries. The delegation’s visit comes as the two countries continue to strengthen bilateral ties across strategic and technology-related sectors. Explore more on these topics Mogadishu Somalia Turkey Related Posts Somalia: Puntland President Warns of Threat to Somalia’s Federal System 2 min read Somalia pledges support for Ugandan businesses as trade ties deepen 3 min read Somali Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre arrives in Jeddah 1 min read Somalia condemns deadly attack on church in Jordan 1 min read Back to top Horseed Media About Profile Contact us Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Category Wararka Soomaaliya Puntland News News Somalia Dowladda Federaalka World News ©2026 Horseed Media Ltd",
